WEBVTT

00:02.585 --> 00:04.337
"Jugemu"?

00:05.046 --> 00:07.716
You mean that one with the long name,
like a tongue-twister?

00:07.799 --> 00:08.800
Right.

00:08.883 --> 00:11.511
That's what I'll perform
at the Karaku Cup.

00:11.594 --> 00:15.306
In that case, wouldn't practicing to talk
fast be better than reading up on it?

00:15.390 --> 00:17.350
That's what you'd think, right?

00:17.434 --> 00:20.520
But lately, I'm starting to get it.

00:21.271 --> 00:22.939
The key to "Jugemu"!

01:53.613 --> 01:57.575
SEVENTH STORY
KARAKU CUP

01:57.659 --> 01:59.494
NOGIKUNIYA HALL

01:59.577 --> 02:01.204
Twenty-eight.

02:01.287 --> 02:02.413
KARAKU CUP PRESS PASS

02:02.497 --> 02:08.670
Kashio-senpai, doesn't this mean there'll
be at least 28 press companies here?

02:08.753 --> 02:09.712
Of course.

02:09.796 --> 02:12.382
Though I hear there'll be
even more tomorrow.

02:12.465 --> 02:14.175
What, even more of them?

02:14.801 --> 02:16.219
What do you think?

02:16.302 --> 02:17.387
Today's just the preliminary round.

02:18.388 --> 02:20.473
They're going to choose the final eight

02:20.557 --> 02:23.601
from the 30 who passed
the document screening.

02:23.685 --> 02:27.856
Issho Arakawa and the other judges
won't be coming till tomorrow.

02:27.939 --> 02:30.316
Still, isn't that a lot of media coverage?

02:30.400 --> 02:33.111
All this for a student oriented event.

02:33.194 --> 02:34.863
Not like it's Koshien or anything.

02:34.946 --> 02:35.780
Nope.

02:35.864 --> 02:37.532
It's Koshien, all right.

02:38.408 --> 02:40.535
The head judge, Issho Arakawa,

02:40.618 --> 02:43.079
now has the strong support
of the entertainment industry.

02:44.080 --> 02:48.459
All you need is Master Issho's stamp of
approval and the jobs'll start coming in.

02:49.043 --> 02:52.380
In fact, his apprentice, Kaisei Arakawa,
reaped those same benefits,

02:52.463 --> 02:54.215
and now he's the top rising star.

02:54.924 --> 02:57.135
Well, since Kaisei's the real deal,

02:57.218 --> 02:59.846
he probably would've succeeded
even without his master.

03:00.680 --> 03:04.017
In other words, this year's Karaku Cup
is no run-of-the-mill event.

03:04.100 --> 03:07.812
It's also an audition
for the next generation's stars!

03:08.521 --> 03:10.899
Doesn't that give you goosebumps?
It does, right?

03:10.982 --> 03:12.567
Of course you've got goosebumps!

03:12.650 --> 03:13.902
You're so tiring.

03:13.985 --> 03:17.906
Yeah, but I'll bet that guy
is the frontrunner this year.

03:18.489 --> 03:21.034
With his free-spirited imagination
and witty elocution,

03:21.117 --> 03:23.703
he won back-to-back Karaku Cups,
last year and the year before.

03:23.786 --> 03:25.538
The prodigy of student Rakugo...

03:26.456 --> 03:27.999
Karashi Nerimaya.

03:28.082 --> 03:29.000
He looks like a flirt.

03:29.626 --> 03:30.835
Seems like he's entering

03:30.919 --> 03:33.671
even though he got accepted
by tons of big-name companies.

03:33.755 --> 03:36.299
Just where do you get that kind of info?

03:37.091 --> 03:38.218
Yeah, I know the type.

03:38.301 --> 03:40.678
The kind of person
who can do anything just like that.

03:41.179 --> 03:44.390
So I guess he's going
to win again this year, huh?

03:44.474 --> 03:45.850
You'd think, right?

03:45.934 --> 03:47.727
This year, aside from Rakugo club people,

03:47.810 --> 03:50.480
a lot of up-and-coming
actors and a voice actress

03:50.563 --> 03:53.233
wanting to be endorsed by Master Issho
will be competing.

03:54.984 --> 03:57.195
And she's the leader of that pack.

03:57.278 --> 03:58.613
Hikaru Koragi.

03:58.696 --> 04:01.241
What? The one who plays Lady Saruel?

04:02.575 --> 04:06.120
Hikaru Koragi plays Saruel on Eden's Nova,

04:06.204 --> 04:08.581
and she's like, the hottest voice actress
right now!

04:08.665 --> 04:11.042
Oh wow, Hikaru's
going to win this for sure!

04:11.125 --> 04:12.543
Of course, she plays Lady Saruel,

04:12.627 --> 04:14.796
but ignoring the fans
who like her for her appearance,

04:14.879 --> 04:15.922
she's good at playing different roles!

04:16.005 --> 04:17.674
And she can show emotion
with just a breath.

04:17.757 --> 04:19.217
She's one of the best actors out there!

04:19.300 --> 04:21.094
So she wouldn't lose to some young newbie.

04:21.177 --> 04:22.512
Too long! Too fast! Shut up!

04:23.096 --> 04:27.433
Anyway, those two should be
the frontrunners for the Karaku Cup.

04:33.022 --> 04:34.732
Holy crap!

04:34.816 --> 04:37.402
Are all voice actresses
these days that pretty?

04:37.485 --> 04:38.528
Whoa!

04:38.611 --> 04:40.154
Are you okay?

04:40.238 --> 04:42.323
You might lose to her.

04:42.407 --> 04:44.158
No way.

04:44.242 --> 04:48.246
Adding your voice to pictures
is nothing like talking on stage.

04:48.830 --> 04:51.291
I'd never lose on my own turf!

04:52.292 --> 04:56.421
Ms. Koragi, that young man
is the defending champion.

04:56.504 --> 04:58.923
Oh, really?
Maybe I should've glared at him.

04:59.007 --> 05:00.008
What?

05:00.091 --> 05:03.720
I'm only kidding.
I'd never do such a thing.

05:04.387 --> 05:06.556
She gives good fan service, too.
I can get behind her!

05:06.639 --> 05:08.725
Cut the crap
and get ready for the interviews.

05:08.808 --> 05:10.018
Oh, yeah?

05:10.101 --> 05:12.061
Who are you going to interview?

05:15.857 --> 05:18.318
- I'm so nervous.
- Me, too.

05:19.694 --> 05:20.778
Excuse me.

05:20.862 --> 05:23.156
You're Ms. Hikaru Koragi, aren't you?

05:23.239 --> 05:24.824
I'm a huge fan of yours!

05:24.907 --> 05:26.993
Um, could you like, shake my hand?

05:28.328 --> 05:29.704
If a handshake will do.

05:32.248 --> 05:33.958
Shake hands with one and it'll never end.

05:34.042 --> 05:36.335
Please be sparing
with the fan service, or...

05:36.419 --> 05:37.879
- Oh, whatever.
- Hey!

05:37.962 --> 05:40.298
Thank you very much!

05:40.381 --> 05:42.133
Is that the voice actress?

05:42.216 --> 05:43.634
What, she's famous?

05:43.718 --> 05:44.594
Who knows?

05:44.677 --> 05:47.263
- She's probably just a hit with otakus.
- I can hear you.

05:48.473 --> 05:49.307
Hey.

05:50.767 --> 05:52.977
- Your obi is a little crooked.
- Huh?

05:54.187 --> 05:56.647
Well, it's hard to tie it yourself, huh?

05:56.731 --> 05:57.857
I'll fix it for you.

05:57.940 --> 05:59.817
Th-Thank you.

06:00.985 --> 06:04.572
She's wearing a man's outfit,
but this girl sure is dexterous.

06:06.240 --> 06:08.409
Good morning!

06:13.539 --> 06:16.793
I'm Kaisei Arakawa,
and I'll be your emcee today.

06:17.293 --> 06:18.920
I'm looking forward
to working with you all.

06:19.003 --> 06:21.464
W-We look forward to working with you!

06:21.547 --> 06:23.841
Jeez, his flair is next-level.

06:23.925 --> 06:25.676
Is he really younger than me?

06:25.760 --> 06:30.473
I'd heard that multiple production
companies have been courting him.

06:30.556 --> 06:32.517
And I can see why they'd want him.

06:32.600 --> 06:34.811
His aura isn't just about his looks.

06:35.311 --> 06:39.232
No wonder he's got the most momentum
of all the up-and-coming Rakugokas.

06:39.732 --> 06:40.733
That's...

06:41.526 --> 06:43.194
Kaisei Arakawa!

06:43.694 --> 06:45.238
Hey, there you are!

06:46.280 --> 06:48.157
Seriously, I was taken aback!

06:53.579 --> 06:55.915
You're looking
at the list of participants again.

06:55.998 --> 06:57.458
Is it bugging you that much?

06:57.542 --> 06:59.752
Well, why wouldn't it bug me?

06:59.836 --> 07:04.340
I mean, the favorite
to win it all in Kaisei's eyes...

07:04.924 --> 07:07.969
Who knew that you'd be competing
in this tournament?

07:08.553 --> 07:10.263
I'm happy to see you again...

07:10.346 --> 07:12.723
...is an unknown female high school student!

07:12.807 --> 07:14.183
...Akane.

07:17.395 --> 07:18.938
Long time no see!

07:19.522 --> 07:20.815
What's up with the boxing stance?

07:20.898 --> 07:22.692
Because last time,
you threw your arms around me!

07:22.775 --> 07:25.945
That's because you performed so well,
I couldn't help myself.

07:26.028 --> 07:27.655
That's not gonna cut it!

07:28.239 --> 07:30.116
Who's that? A college student?

07:30.199 --> 07:31.742
Nah, I don't think so.

07:31.826 --> 07:33.369
Don't tell me she's in high school?

07:33.953 --> 07:35.496
They seem so close.

07:35.580 --> 07:37.915
Not only that, but it
looks like he's acknowledged her talent?

07:37.999 --> 07:39.542
Who is this girl?

07:39.625 --> 07:41.002
But you know what?

07:41.085 --> 07:44.922
After what you told me that day,
and if you're entering this competition,

07:45.006 --> 07:49.427
means you've reconsidered taking me up
on my invitation to train under my master,

07:50.636 --> 07:53.222
or you crave attention from the industry.

07:54.599 --> 07:56.559
I have no interest in either.

07:59.020 --> 08:01.481
There's something I'd like to ask
Issho Arakawa.

08:03.858 --> 08:06.611
That's why I'm here! No other reason.

08:08.070 --> 08:10.907
You're talking about the sit-down
with the winner?

08:10.990 --> 08:12.950
Then, losing's not an option, huh?

08:13.743 --> 08:14.994
Of course not.

08:15.077 --> 08:17.705
For my part, it's not like
I've been playing around since that day.

08:18.706 --> 08:21.209
I have no intention of losing,
no matter who I'm up against.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.545
THE VENUE IS NOW OPEN
PLEASE COME THIS WAY TO SIGN IN

08:27.632 --> 08:29.258
Are you looking for somebody?

08:29.342 --> 08:32.220
Well, Akane asked me
to do something for her.

08:32.303 --> 08:34.972
But all she sent me
was this terrible sketch.

08:35.973 --> 08:36.849
What the hell?

08:36.933 --> 08:39.101
Hey, that person...

08:41.145 --> 08:43.523
Excuse me, are you Iwashimizu-sensei?

08:43.606 --> 08:44.982
Uh, yes.

08:45.066 --> 08:48.277
I'm Guriko Arakawa,
Akane's elder fellow apprentice.

08:48.361 --> 08:50.655
She asked me to show you around today.

08:50.738 --> 08:53.950
If you have any questions,
please ask me anything.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.451
Oh.

08:55.535 --> 08:56.577
GLASSES, KINDA MAD
IWA-SENSEI

08:56.661 --> 08:58.579
She actually has her features down.

08:59.497 --> 09:01.082
That's right!

09:01.165 --> 09:04.961
Even if it were true, he's the kind of guy
who'd let someone swipe his wife.

09:05.545 --> 09:07.004
Are you coming, too?

09:07.088 --> 09:09.924
My elder fellow apprentices
will be there, so I'll let them know.

09:10.508 --> 09:12.677
I don't know how this happened.

09:13.886 --> 09:17.598
Not bad, is it? Listening to amateurs'
Rakugo once in a while?

09:17.682 --> 09:21.310
That was Chusuke Chuotei's
"The Pocket Book."

09:21.394 --> 09:23.354
I wonder what kind of "Jugemu"
she'll be doing?

09:23.437 --> 09:24.855
You didn't ask her?

09:24.939 --> 09:26.023
No.

09:26.107 --> 09:28.568
But the other day,
when I saw her, she told me.

09:29.860 --> 09:32.446
That she'd finally turned Jugemu
into words.

09:34.448 --> 09:38.160
And now, let's move on
to the next participant.

09:39.203 --> 09:40.580
Let's see what you're made of.

09:42.582 --> 09:45.251
A third year at Ryokugyoku High School.

09:48.212 --> 09:49.463
This is Akane!

09:55.052 --> 09:56.470
AKANE

09:57.471 --> 09:59.348
I'm finally starting to understand.

10:00.474 --> 10:04.437
Talking fast isn't the key to "Jugemu."

10:05.896 --> 10:08.899
So, in a world where
lies and falsehoods abound,

10:08.983 --> 10:10.860
the preciousness of children
is a universal truth.

10:10.943 --> 10:12.528
At least, that's what they say.

10:12.612 --> 10:14.947
They also say that you'll never
understand that preciousness

10:15.031 --> 10:16.490
until you've had your own child
to cherish.

10:16.574 --> 10:20.119
Since time immemorial,
whenever a child is born,

10:20.202 --> 10:22.496
it's always been the father's job
to name them.

10:22.580 --> 10:25.041
Listen, dear. What are we going to do?

10:25.124 --> 10:27.168
It's been nearly seven days
since the baby was born.

10:27.251 --> 10:29.337
Oh, yeah. What about it?

10:29.420 --> 10:30.421
Don't be silly.

10:30.504 --> 10:32.423
The seventh night
is the Oshichiya naming ceremony.

10:32.506 --> 10:34.175
Oshichiya!

10:34.258 --> 10:35.384
Well, I didn't know that.

10:35.468 --> 10:38.512
- Why don't you go to the temple...
- No signs of nervousness.

10:40.139 --> 10:42.433
This venue's capacity is 600 people, max.

10:42.516 --> 10:44.894
There are nearly 400 here today.

10:44.977 --> 10:48.814
Even though she's facing way more people
than she did at the Rakugo Café...

10:48.898 --> 10:51.901
No, that's not true.
If the monks at the temple...

10:51.984 --> 10:54.028
"I haven't been playing around."

10:55.321 --> 10:57.740
Looks like she's put in the work
to back up those words.

10:58.366 --> 11:00.951
Well, he grew up healthy and strong,

11:01.035 --> 11:03.871
and he couldn't have been more
rambunctious, and getting into fights.

11:03.954 --> 11:07.249
Compared to the other students,
it's as clear as day.

11:08.501 --> 11:11.921
That girl stands head and shoulders
above others of her generation.

11:14.715 --> 11:18.844
Even so, winning with "Jugemu"
is still a harsh ask.

11:19.345 --> 11:20.596
Though it looks like

11:20.679 --> 11:23.432
she figured something out
thanks to Koguma Ani-san's advice.

11:23.933 --> 11:29.397
...paipo-paipo-paipo
no shuringan, shuringan no gurindai

11:29.480 --> 11:34.443
Gurindai no ponpoko-na no ponpoko-pi
no chokyumei-no-chosuke

11:34.527 --> 11:37.113
hit me on the head,
and gave me this big lump!

11:37.196 --> 11:39.740
How will she change her enunciation?

11:39.824 --> 11:41.325
Are you saying my son

11:41.409 --> 11:43.452
Jugemu jugemu goko-no-surikirezu
kaijari-suigyo no suigyomatsu

11:43.536 --> 11:45.621
ungyomatsu furaimatsu
kuu-neru tokoro ni sumu tokoro

11:45.704 --> 11:49.417
Yaburakoji no burakoji paipo-paipo-paipo
no shuringan, shuringan no gurindai

11:49.500 --> 11:52.503
Gurindai no ponpoko-na no ponpoko-pi
no chokyumei-no-chosuke

11:52.586 --> 11:54.755
hit you on the head and gave you a lump?

11:54.839 --> 11:56.298
Hey, honey! Did you hear that?

11:56.382 --> 11:57.508
Our son Jugemu jugemu goko-no-surikirezu...

11:57.591 --> 11:59.301
So fast!

11:59.385 --> 12:02.096
No, her wordplay's sharper
than it was in the park.

12:02.179 --> 12:04.265
But, she's totally ignoring
Ani-san's advice?

12:04.348 --> 12:06.267
She's got some guts.

12:06.350 --> 12:07.476
...hit Maa-chan on the head.

12:07.560 --> 12:09.645
Yes, it's so you can win.

12:09.728 --> 12:12.064
But you're staking the prelims
on your enunciation alone.

12:12.148 --> 12:14.900
Jugemu jugemu goko-no-surikirezu
kaijari-suigyo no suigyomatsu furai...

12:14.984 --> 12:16.193
Even faster now!

12:17.111 --> 12:19.572
Not only that, but she's even
taking less breaths now.

12:19.655 --> 12:21.699
That gives more momentum to her words.

12:22.700 --> 12:24.326
Still, with those long lines...

12:25.161 --> 12:27.705
I'm going to win the Karaku Cup
with only "Jugemu."

12:28.789 --> 12:33.502
To do that, I'm winning today
on my enunciation, and nothing else!

12:36.797 --> 12:40.843
Well, his name was so long,
the lump healed up!

12:45.723 --> 12:48.142
Wasn't that incredible?
And she's a high school kid!

12:48.225 --> 12:50.811
That was insane. She's like a pro, huh?

12:53.022 --> 12:56.275
As a pro, what did you think
of Ms. Osaki's Rakugo?

12:56.358 --> 12:59.695
Huh? Oh. Well, I'd say it wasn't half bad.

12:59.778 --> 13:02.156
No, it wasn't! That's what I thought, too.

13:02.948 --> 13:06.118
I've seen her practicing
with jump ropes a lot lately.

13:06.202 --> 13:09.830
That must've been her way of building up
her lung power.

13:10.414 --> 13:12.124
She's actually passionate, huh?

13:12.708 --> 13:14.585
Great job, Ms. Osaki.

13:15.169 --> 13:16.921
I think victory's within reach!

13:19.590 --> 13:22.009
Oh, not a chance. Not by a long shot.

13:22.092 --> 13:24.553
What? But wasn't she crazy good?

13:24.637 --> 13:26.472
Oh, I'll give you that.

13:26.555 --> 13:29.308
But you know what, that's like
an incredibly talented singer

13:29.391 --> 13:31.519
singing a children's song,
don't you think?

13:32.269 --> 13:36.273
Would we start getting emotional
if we heard a kid's song now?

13:36.357 --> 13:38.567
I mean, the supply and demand don't mesh.

13:38.651 --> 13:41.445
From a marketing standpoint,
that was the worst possible choice.

13:41.529 --> 13:43.113
Way too naïve.

13:43.697 --> 13:50.037
In the first place, people who just mimic
ancient stories are no threat to me.

13:50.538 --> 13:55.417
I mean, she's free to go ahead and add
some luster to my legend, you know?

13:58.754 --> 14:00.798
Good job. Have some, if you'd like.

14:01.799 --> 14:03.092
What? Are you sure?

14:03.175 --> 14:05.678
- Yes. To thank you for my obi.
- Thanks!

14:06.262 --> 14:08.138
My throat is so parched!

14:11.267 --> 14:14.562
I looked her up online,
but there was nothing on this girl.

14:15.479 --> 14:17.273
She's cute and she's talented.

14:17.940 --> 14:20.150
An unknown high school girl,
younger than me,

14:20.234 --> 14:22.903
who's drawn the attention
of Kaisei Arakawa.

14:23.487 --> 14:25.823
She's bursting with elements
that social media sheep would love.

14:26.824 --> 14:30.661
But now I know for sure
who my competition is.

14:31.662 --> 14:34.248
To surpass her in every way.

14:34.331 --> 14:35.165
That...

14:35.249 --> 14:39.587
is the minimum condition for me
to take the spotlight at the Karaku Cup.

14:43.382 --> 14:44.925
The Karaku Cup preliminary round

14:45.009 --> 14:47.177
is a cutthroat battle
like nothing we've ever seen before.

14:48.220 --> 14:50.598
And the participants
who are drawing the most attention are

14:51.432 --> 14:54.143
the winner of the previous tournament,
Karashi Nerimaya,

14:54.727 --> 14:56.854
the popular voice actress, Hikaru Koragi,

14:57.563 --> 14:58.522
and...

14:59.106 --> 15:00.649
despite being an unknown
high school student,

15:00.733 --> 15:03.736
her soaring talent
kept the audience riveted.

15:04.486 --> 15:05.696
Akane.

15:06.447 --> 15:08.574
The eight participants,
including these three,

15:08.657 --> 15:12.328
have advanced to the final round,
where Master Issho Arakawa awaits them.

15:15.205 --> 15:18.584
The final round is going to be wild.

15:21.128 --> 15:25.049
Ms. Osaki, congratulations on advancing
past the Karaku Cup preliminary round!

15:25.132 --> 15:25.966
Thanks!

15:26.050 --> 15:28.177
That said, it's still just the prelims.

15:28.260 --> 15:29.762
The final round is tomorrow.

15:29.845 --> 15:31.597
Don't let this go to your head.

15:31.680 --> 15:34.266
Please get some rest
and rejuvenate yourself tonight.

15:34.350 --> 15:35.434
Right!

15:35.517 --> 15:37.561
She sounds like a coach.

15:37.645 --> 15:40.940
Hey, where did Koguma Ani-san go?

15:41.523 --> 15:43.525
- He left already.
- He left?

15:44.151 --> 15:45.986
"Just because I say something to her,

15:46.070 --> 15:47.947
doesn't mean that
anything will change, right?"

15:48.030 --> 15:49.073
And such.

15:49.156 --> 15:50.616
Is that right?

15:51.825 --> 15:56.580
Yes, but he didn't leave until after he'd
seen you advance to the final round.

15:57.331 --> 15:59.416
He may seem cold and aloof,

15:59.500 --> 16:02.920
but I think he's looking out for you,
Ms. Osaki.

16:03.921 --> 16:06.507
Even the fact that he left must be
his way of hiding his embarrassment.

16:06.590 --> 16:08.592
He should be more honest about it.

16:08.676 --> 16:10.302
You're one to talk.

16:10.886 --> 16:15.099
Still, I'm impressed that you
delivered such long lines so fast.

16:15.182 --> 16:16.517
Huh? Well,

16:17.309 --> 16:19.853
I memorized "Jugemu"
back when I was four or five.

16:19.937 --> 16:21.313
You were doing Rakugo at that age?

16:22.231 --> 16:25.985
Actually, it was more like
a kind of tongue-twister.

16:28.112 --> 16:31.031
My dad taught it to me.

16:33.826 --> 16:36.787
Is that right? Will he be coming tomorrow?

16:36.870 --> 16:38.372
Oh, no, he won't be coming.

16:38.455 --> 16:41.125
He's on a business trip,
so he's not even in Tokyo.

16:41.208 --> 16:44.628
All right, why don't we call it a day now?

16:44.712 --> 16:46.922
I bet she's exhausted.

16:47.006 --> 16:48.507
You're right.

16:48.590 --> 16:49.591
See ya.

16:50.843 --> 16:51.802
Don't get too worked up, now.

16:53.512 --> 16:54.763
Thanks!

16:54.847 --> 16:56.598
Hey, my sensu!

16:56.682 --> 16:58.559
Did I leave it in the dressing room?

16:58.642 --> 17:00.227
All right, see you!

17:06.775 --> 17:10.654
So Ms. Osaki's been exposed
to Rakugo since she was a child.

17:11.405 --> 17:16.160
If she wins, she'll get to speak
with Master Issho Arakawa,

17:16.243 --> 17:19.997
and he might help her
to succeed as a Rakugoka.

17:22.708 --> 17:24.752
I usually don't like to do this,

17:24.835 --> 17:27.087
but you shouldn't be
the only one who doesn't know.

17:28.047 --> 17:29.048
The thing is...

17:34.178 --> 17:35.888
There it is. Thank goodness!

17:35.971 --> 17:37.056
Come on, now!

17:37.848 --> 17:42.478
I've gotta tournament I gotta win
today and tomorrow, no matter what!

17:42.561 --> 17:44.521
And I wanna focus!

17:44.605 --> 17:47.733
To keep going in this line of work,
I gotta be more popular.

17:47.816 --> 17:51.153
Right! If I'm not on my toes,
no work will come my way.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.489
And that's because...

17:56.283 --> 17:58.660
I-Isn't that your fault, Mother?

17:59.328 --> 18:01.538
Wh-What's she doing here?

18:01.622 --> 18:04.625
I made sure everyone
had left before I called.

18:05.209 --> 18:07.086
Yes. All right, I'm hanging up now.

18:07.169 --> 18:08.921
I'm hanging up. Bye now.

18:09.671 --> 18:11.298
Did she hear my dialect?

18:11.381 --> 18:12.549
No, hard to tell.

18:12.633 --> 18:14.760
Stay calm. Act like nothing happened.

18:14.843 --> 18:15.886
Is something the matter?

18:15.969 --> 18:18.263
What was that
rapid-fire chattering just now?

18:18.347 --> 18:21.350
I like it! Was that a dialect?
Where are you from?

18:22.267 --> 18:23.602
Damn it all.

18:24.645 --> 18:25.854
Oh, wow.

18:25.938 --> 18:27.856
So you're from Fukuoka?

18:27.940 --> 18:29.274
Fukuoka's great, huh?

18:29.358 --> 18:31.110
The way you end your sentences is so cute!

18:31.193 --> 18:32.611
Thanks.

18:32.694 --> 18:34.071
Oh, please stop already.

18:34.154 --> 18:36.198
I wanted to give off the aura
of a city woman.

18:36.281 --> 18:38.700
You're a voice actress, right, Hikaru?

18:38.784 --> 18:40.953
I think it's awesome that
you can do Rakugo, too.

18:41.036 --> 18:43.288
Well, I could say the same
about you, Akane.

18:43.372 --> 18:46.291
Oh, but my dad was a Rakugoka, so...

18:46.959 --> 18:47.876
Oh?

18:48.627 --> 18:50.420
So you learned Rakugo from your father?

18:50.504 --> 18:54.049
No, it's more like
I learned by watching my dad.

18:54.133 --> 18:57.302
I'm actually learning from Dad's master.

18:57.386 --> 18:58.428
Master.

18:59.429 --> 19:01.223
So you're being trained by a professional?

19:01.306 --> 19:02.558
Right.

19:02.641 --> 19:06.436
I really had to push hard to get
permission to enter this tournament,

19:07.229 --> 19:10.274
so tomorrow I have to make sure
my Rakugo lives up to my master's name.

19:11.275 --> 19:12.234
I see.

19:12.818 --> 19:14.695
Well, I'm heading home now.

19:14.778 --> 19:16.446
Sorry I interrupted your phone call.

19:16.530 --> 19:18.323
No, no. See you.

19:23.745 --> 19:26.206
She's young, pretty, and talented.

19:26.790 --> 19:29.001
She's drawn the attention
of Kaisei Arakawa,

19:29.084 --> 19:31.003
and she's training under a professional.

19:31.086 --> 19:33.172
A second-generation Rakugoka
high school student.

19:33.755 --> 19:36.466
She knows that she's better than others,

19:36.550 --> 19:38.844
which is why she has the confidence
to win with "Jugemu."

19:39.720 --> 19:41.013
I see.

19:41.513 --> 19:42.723
What is this?

19:43.223 --> 19:44.725
She's super annoying!

19:45.225 --> 19:47.686
She's the one person I won't lose to!

19:48.937 --> 19:51.315
It's all right. You did your best.

19:51.899 --> 19:54.067
Let's go home, okay?

19:55.027 --> 19:57.863
It really is a student event, huh?

19:58.447 --> 20:00.324
There's a passion
that you don't see at the theaters.

20:00.407 --> 20:02.409
Why do you always show up out of the blue?

20:02.492 --> 20:03.827
Just a coincidence!

20:04.411 --> 20:06.997
Your "Jugemu" was awesome today, too.

20:07.080 --> 20:09.082
I think it was a good enough warm-up.

20:09.166 --> 20:10.542
Huh? Wait, why...

20:10.626 --> 20:12.794
Was I right?

20:12.878 --> 20:16.006
I had a feeling, but it's worth
tricking people into confessing.

20:16.089 --> 20:17.007
This guy...

20:17.090 --> 20:19.927
But hey,
if that was you going for the kill,

20:20.594 --> 20:22.429
I'd just have to write you off.

20:23.430 --> 20:26.391
You can write me off,
and it wouldn't make me sad in the least.

20:26.475 --> 20:27.809
Wow, that's tough!

20:28.393 --> 20:30.646
But I guess it's just as tough for you.

20:30.729 --> 20:32.564
I mean, it's "Jugemu."

20:33.148 --> 20:34.816
I told you before, didn't I?

20:34.900 --> 20:37.110
That you'd catch up to me in no time.

20:38.487 --> 20:42.699
If that's still your goal, then it won't
be enough to win this tournament.

20:43.951 --> 20:47.329
You need to blow my master away.

20:47.412 --> 20:50.540
I don't need you to tell me that.

20:51.458 --> 20:53.752
Is that right? Then it's all good.

20:54.586 --> 20:55.712
See you.

20:55.796 --> 20:58.173
I'll be looking forward
to your performance tomorrow.

21:00.592 --> 21:02.219
Easier said than done.

21:02.719 --> 21:05.555
Akane, do you...

21:06.056 --> 21:08.475
have what it takes
to rip off my master's mask?

21:10.227 --> 21:13.105
- Whatever it takes, I have to win!
- Winning won't be enough.

21:13.188 --> 21:14.398
I'll be fine.

21:14.481 --> 21:15.899
Don't let this go to your head.

21:15.983 --> 21:17.234
It hasn't gone to my head.

21:18.235 --> 21:19.611
I'm going to win tomorrow!

21:22.781 --> 21:23.615
I have to win.

21:25.117 --> 21:26.660
Or I won't be able to grasp anything.

21:36.545 --> 21:38.714
Look at all these photographers!

21:38.797 --> 21:41.341
Well, in a sense, the main character
will be showing up today.

21:41.425 --> 21:42.426
Here he is!

21:43.010 --> 21:44.386
Master Issho has arrived.

21:44.469 --> 21:46.096
Thank you for coming!

21:46.638 --> 21:47.514
Hello.

21:52.352 --> 21:54.146
Well, well.

21:54.730 --> 21:56.273
So early in the morning...

21:56.356 --> 21:59.192
Just look at this huge turnout!

21:59.276 --> 22:02.988
KARAKU CUP - FINAL ROUND
BEGINS

23:36.331 --> 23:37.958
NEXT EPISODE
WHAT THEY WANT

23:38.834 --> 23:40.502
Akane Small Talk!

23:46.258 --> 23:48.468
I just can't seem to fold it right.

23:49.052 --> 23:52.722
Hey, want me to show you
how to fold a kimono neatly?

23:52.806 --> 23:55.142
Huh? Uh, yes.

23:55.225 --> 23:56.476
Let me see.

23:56.977 --> 24:00.772
If you fold a kimono
along its original folds and stitches,

24:00.856 --> 24:02.315
you can fold it straight and neat.

24:03.942 --> 24:05.735
After you've folded the hemline,

24:06.695 --> 24:09.739
then you bring both sides of the collar
together, then fold the sleeves.

24:13.577 --> 24:15.996
And now you just make it compact.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.040
There, it's done!

24:19.124 --> 24:21.543
See? If you do it this way,
you can fold it neatly, right?

24:21.626 --> 24:24.087
You're right! Thanks!

24:24.671 --> 24:26.756
Here. Now you try it yourself!

24:26.840 --> 24:28.842
- What?
- All right, good work today! Good luck!

24:32.053 --> 24:33.597
So annoying.
